p.src:
A cautious reconstruction of the compounding model is $\begin{aligned}
K_{t+1}&=K_t+L_t,\\
Y_{t+k}&=f\!\left(\sum_{i\le t} L_i\right),\end{aligned}$ where $L_t$ is one learning input and $Y_t$ is later revenue or business output. The point is not that the speaker literally presents such a formula. The point is that his spoken explanation has exactly this structure: many earlier learning inputs accumulate, and a later mastermind or mentorship may act as the catalyst without being the sole cause.

